Vivienne, with Pallister's findings in hand I think we can close this out. =
The cause was the failed condensate drain above the corridor ceiling, not t=
he slab and not the flooring assembly. Ledgerwood measured the substrate at=
 71 to 74 percent relative humidity and confirmed the epoxy mitigation film=
 was continuous and well bonded.<br />
<br />
Our recommendation is to rebuild the drain and pan first, dry the wall cavi=
ty and the topping slab for a minimum of fourteen days with monitoring, and=
 then replace plank across the affected band plus three feet in every direc=
tion. We will provide the repair detail and a revised transition at the pan=
try threshold at no charge.<br />
<br />
For the record, VAA is not asserting and does not expect to assert any clai=
m on this, and we do not read your building as having a moisture problem. I=
t had a plumbing problem.